WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Someone that I am a fan o
and I'm going to guess,

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.703
based on his presence in the
film, you're also a fan of

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:10.210
is Action Bronson, who fully
steals a scene that he's in.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.177 size:88% position:44% line:92%
How is working with him?

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.113 size:78% position:39%
And was that someone,
again, that you had

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.280 line:92%
in mind since the beginning?

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was one of those guys
that just came in

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.852 line:92%
and just crushed the audition.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:22.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was just so funny.
And we just had to have him.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.124 line:92%
And he was -- He's a blast

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's just a really fun guy
to have on set.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.428 size:81% position:41%
And he's definitely an
interesting character,

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.029 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to say the least.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:32.198
-Yeah. It was funny -- the las
time we had him on the show,

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.801
he was talking about how
he was in "The Irishman,"

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I kind of
couldn't believe.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was really good
in that, too.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.806 line:92%
I'm like, "Wow, Action Bronson

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
two for two
right out of the gate."

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.910
-Yeah. "The Irishman" and
"The King of Staten Island

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the same year
is pretty incredible.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:49.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-Also, couldn't care less.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, just, like, walked in,
just crushes it.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.721 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's ridiculous.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.322 line:92%
-Just rolls out right after.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will say Action Bronson --
always been

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:03.129
a great guest on our show,
and we're never quite sure

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.365 size:78% position:39%
he's going to show up
till the last minute.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.434 line:92%
And he's never let us down

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Same on our set.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had no idea if
he was ever gonna come,

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.705
and he showed up and just
knocked it out of the park

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we're very grateful
for that.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's incredible
the patience you will have

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.545 size:88% position:44% line:92%
with people who deliver.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:19.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:25.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You play an aspiring
tattoo artist in the film.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
You obviously have tattoos
of your own.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.756
Is this something -- Have yo
ever given one in real life?

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've given a couple to
my friends, like,

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
little, tiny tattoos
with like, words and stuff

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:38.098
but nothing too crazy, because I
have a shaky hand, I was told.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:38.498 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it's not really great
for tattooing.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. It would seem like
that's, like, the way they -

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
It would be like, if you'r
afraid of the water,

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:50.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
they'd probably say, you know,
"Swimming's not for you."

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is a scene
where you work in a restaurant

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:57.750
and people fight for tips, like,
physically fight for tips.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this something you pulled
from your own life?

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:06.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When I used to work at
my uncle's Italian restaurant,

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:09.896
if there was ever, like,
a beef with another co-worker --

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wouldn't be for tips,
but if there was ever a beef

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.735 size:81% position:41%
he thought it would be
a great idea to have

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hulk hands and boxing gloves
after work,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you and your co-worker
can duke it out.

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:24.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, whoever win
wins the argument.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.981
And I got into one of thos
fights and I got annihilated

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:30.817
so I just thought it would b
funny to throw in the movie.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is it -- It was --
in real life,

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:32.986 line:92%
did you do it the same way

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you do it in the center of
the restaurant after hours

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.824
-Yeah. They just cleared
everything out of the way

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were like,
"Alright, Pete, you're up.

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope it was
worth that argument

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.229 line:92%
you had earlier at 9:00 a.m.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the thing is, like,
when you have like

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:47.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
a 12-hour work day,
something you have at night,

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're like, "I don't even
care anymore.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to get
my ass kicked."

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:53.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Well, that's like -
I would say, like --

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
At "SNL," my theory was, if yo
were upset about something

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:58.545 line:92%
don't bring it up at the party

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
See if you're still mad
by Monday.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:03.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the reality is, like,
time makes everything

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.185 line:92%
seem petty, which is helpful

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.886 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right. Yeah.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:10.256 line:92%
-Do you -- You guys did three,

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess,
social-distancing shows.

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:15.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
You managed to do a song
with Adam Sandler

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:18.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
about being stuck at home,
which was fantastic.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:21.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, certainly
a hero of mine.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.369 size:88% position:44% line:92%
How did that come about?

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:26.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm pretty tight with
"The Sand Man,"

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:30.476
which is the coolest thing
I think, I ever get to say

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is just such a cool,
nice guy.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:35.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't explain how wonderfu
of a person he is.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:38.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just reached out
and texted him and was like,

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:41.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, is there any shot
you would ever

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:42.488 line:92%
want to do a song together?"

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was like,
"Hell yeah, buddy."

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:45.291 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it was awesome.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we just sent each othe
notes and stuff back and forth

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he came up with
that great verse.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:54.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it just fell together.
I was really thrilled.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He is -- It is one of the -
I think, you know,

00:03:57.337 --> 00:04:00.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
when people ask you,
"Who are the nicest people

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've met that are
celebrities?",

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.611
it's really fun to be able t
tell them that Adam Sandle

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:07.447
is truly one of the nicest
human beings they can meet

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
People are very happy
to hear that,

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:11.117
because I think they would b
heartbroken if he was a bad guy,

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.452 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and it is the opposite.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.119 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.654 line:92%
Yeah, he's definitely the best

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just, like,
very caring and sweet

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:19.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
and actually not full of crap,
which is very rare to find

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:25.198
-Back when you guys were doing
the in-studio shows last season,

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:26.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you have
a personal favorite?

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.668 size:78% position:39%
Was there a highlight
for you last year?

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:32.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My favorite was
the Mulaney show,

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:34.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we got to do another
one of those

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.309 line:92%
bodega-bathroom-type things.

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:39.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we had just -- I just love
those musical numbers.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:42.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's really fun to hav
like a 12-minute sketch

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.883 size:84% position:42% line:92%
that's just ridiculous.

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's always fun
to work with Mulaney.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he's
the greatest, as well.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:53.293
-It's also very fun that you are
such an essential cog

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.560 line:92%
to this trilogy of musicals now.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, really, without
your character's bad decisions

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
we'd never hear
any of these songs.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:04.504 line:92%
-Right. It's all up to me.

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:06.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Buddy, congrats again
on the movie.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.408 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's fantastic.

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:09.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:10.376 line:92%
It's always nice to see you.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:11.878 size:78% position:39%
Hopefully, next time,
it'll be in person.

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:13.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks for having me, Seth.
I appreciate it.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:14.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hope to see you soon.
-Alright.

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:19.052
Say hello to your mother for me.
-Alright, I will.

